{{Story head|[[Theresa]] sees everything in the [[Doctor]]'s memories, and finally completes her farewell to ''that particular person.''}}
{{sc|Light|mode=backgroundimg}}
{{sc|Erasing memories. This is something [[Theresa]] actually lacks experience in.<br/>Not to mention she now faces a rare kind of mind.<br/>She knows not what she will see, and has no clue if it will be dangerous. But there is no room to retreat.<br/>She has made the final decision of her life.<br/>She walks into the [[Doctor]]'s memories, and cuts them up into countless fragments of dissipating threads.<br/>Memory fades away in silence.<br/>She walks through a world she has never seen and could never understand.<br/>How did such a glorious civilization meet its end?<br/>How do geniuses as bright as shooting stars struggle for a solution to their ultimate problem, yet find nothing?<br/>Is resistance futile? Is unity a mere fantasy?<br/>Is [[Terra]]'s future already set in stone? What of her beloved homeland?<br/>What of her loved ones?<br/>She has no answer. She cannot find the answer.<br/>She can only continue meandering in the void of memories gone.<br/>Finally, she sees someone familiar.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|1|mode=background}}
{{sc|The sound of party poppers, cheers, and chatter fill the air. [[Kal'tsit]] walks up next to the Doctor.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Is all their enthusiasm overwhelming you?}}
{{sc|Doctor|What brings you here, Kal'tsit?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Should I not be present at this celebration of your latest victory?}}
{{sc|Doctor|It's been a long time since I last... days like these were rare back then, you know.<br/>Or I should say, I've grown so unaccustomed to it now.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|No matter, you will get used to it again, in time. Babel will be a new beginning.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit smiles tenderly.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Go. We should enjoy this celebration.}}
{{sc|Theresa watches Kal'tsit pat the Doctor before gently pushing that very back into the waiting crowd.<br/>Too many are forcing their way through the throng, hands stretched out, fighting each other to be the first to shake the Doctor's hand, or pat the Doctor's shoulder.<br/>Some taller and gutsier ones even try to put their hands right on the Doctor's head for a good kneading.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|...?}}
{{sc|Scout|Uh, sorry about that unruly subordinate of mine, Doctor. I wanted to stop him...<br/>But my arm's injured... so I couldn't make it in time.}}
{{sc|Doctor|It's fine... how's your arm?}}
{{sc|Scout|Recovery's going pretty well.}}
{{sc|Doctor|It's a pity you won't get to enjoy many drinks here tonight.}}
{{sc|[[Ace]] walks up next to [[Scout]].|mode=action}}
{{sc|Ace|That's alright, Doctor. I'll have a few more pints on this guy's behalf.<br/>We might have gotten ourselves stuck in that encirclement, had you not sprung that surprise attack at the end.<br/>C'mon, let's slam a few glasses to honor the Doctor!}}
{{sc|Doctor|I'm afraid my alcohol tolerance may disappoint you, Ace.}}
{{sc|[[Closure]] runs up next to them.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Closure|Excuuuuse—me,—make—way please... I have to see the protagonist of the day!<br/>So many people in here! This is the first time I feel that the command center is too small... do you want me to widen it later? There's still so many people outside hurrying in here with snacks and drinks.}}
{{sc|Logos|Doctor, everyone's cheering for the victory you've brought us, but you seem a little... uneasy.}}
{{sc|Doctor|I thought I was masking it pretty well. *ahem* I'm just a little nervous in crowds.}}
{{sc|Scout stumbles a bit.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Scout|Hey, careful. That's enough pushing. [[Amiya]], you good?}}
{{sc|Amiya|I'm okay!<br/>Doctor! Come with me, Theresa and I made you a cake!<br/>Look, the oven was so hot I got a blister on my finger.}}
{{sc|Doctor|Thank you... Oh! Are you okay? Does anyone have some burn cream...?}}
{{sc|A gentle cough sounds in the room, and the crowd splits into two.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|The crowd falls silent.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresa sees a woman dressed in white passing by, smiling as she extends a hand to the Doctor with a still healing needle wound.<br/>She is looking at herself.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Light|mode=backgroundimg}}
{{sc|The joy fades away, as do the memories and voices.<br/>Theresa erases the memory she is too familiar with, and continues forward.<br/>She sees a record she has never seen before within [[PRTS]].|mode=speech}}
{{sc|2|mode=background}}
{{sc|The Doctor steps into an empty room.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Doctor|Invoke imaging capabilities. Enable administrator-level encryption.<br/>Image number (0091_admin)...... Add subject: (This is for you).<br/>Activating recorder... Beginning video record.}}
{{sc|glitches|mode=background}}
{{sc|becomes tinted green with noise as recording activates|mode=background}}
{{sc|Doctor|......<br/>If I didn't hold on until you woke up, you'll see this video.<br/>I will remain here, in the safest of places until everything settles.<br/>Once I'm done with everything, I'll vanish into silence...<br/>Disappearing before all those who hate me.<br/>......<br/>There is always a voice inside me, reminding me, asking me—"Who am I?"<br/>Our own watcher? Or a traitor to future civilizations?<br/>I can no longer recognize myself—<br/>You'll get an answer after checking all the logs I left behind. But for now at least, I'll no longer hesitate to do what I should do.<br/>...I...<br/>When you wake up, I will have already disappeared in your past, and also unable to appear in our promised future.<br/>That's why I hope...<br/>...Pause recording. Delete all previous content. I... still need a bit more time.}}
{{sc|Light|mode=backgroundimg}}
{{sc|Theresa|......}}
{{sc|She does not pause or sigh, just continues what she ought to do in silence.<br/>Theresa goes deeper into the buried memories.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|3|mode=background}}
{{sc|tinted red|mode=background}}
{{sc|The Doctor is calling emergency services while standing next to a burning vehicle.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Doctor|I need you to contact the closest rescue team! The wrecked transport has a [[Rim Billiton]] logo on it, this is your squad...<br/>I hear someone still alive in there!}}
{{sc|Comms|*bzzt* We got your call, but it'll take some time for us to rush over from the nearest mining plate.<br/>Based on the information you gave us, there's been banditry at your location there before, so we'll also notify armed security to send a dispatch at once.}}
{{sc|???|...Ugh...}}
{{sc|Doctor|...Armed security...? But with the way Rim Billiton treats [[Infected]] orphans...<br/>Hmph—}}
{{sc|The Doctor ends the call and decides to climb onto the burning transport.|mode=action}}
{{sc|49_i20_1|mode=image}}
{{sc|Doctor|Just hold on... I'll get you out of there myself...}}
{{sc|???|...You...}}
{{sc|Doctor|Please, stay with me... gah... that's a good girl, give me your hand.<br/>Hold tight!}}
{{sc|???|But... I'm so... tired...}}
{{sc|Doctor|What's your name—}}
{{sc|???|...I—<br/>Name...?}}
{{sc|49_i20_2|mode=image}}
{{sc|???|Mum... calls me... Amiya...}}
{{sc|Doctor|Amiya, just hold on tight!}}
{{sc|Amiya|I... I'm holding—}}
{{sc|Doctor|I won't let go—}}
{{sc|fades to white|mode=background}}
{{sc|The memory shatters.<br/>This is Theresa's destination, the terminus of the Doctor's memory—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|"Theresa..."|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresa|......<br/>This is impossible. Every memory should have been...}}
{{sc|"Theresa."|mode=speech}}
{{sc|She follows the voice to a void, and it speaks once more from behind the nothingness.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresa|Where am I—}}
{{sc|4|mode=background}}
{{sc|Theresa stands in the middle of some grassy fields.|mode=action}}
{{sc|???|You're finally here. I've been waiting for you.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Doctor...?}}
{{sc|???|Doctor?<br/>Not many people call me that. They prefer my team codename—"Oracle".}}
{{sc|Theresa|...Oracle...<br/>So you're the one Kal'tsit believes in.}}
{{sc|Oracle|I've let her down terribly. But we had no choice, I'm entangled in an inescapable plot.<br/>I've been watching you from here as you went around nurturing your hopes, as you suffered betrayal—<br/>As if I was looking at my past self.}}
{{sc|Theresa|...I'm sorry.<br/>You are only residue of the Doctor's burned away emotions. There's no way for me to preserve your emotions and memories in our current circumstances...}}
{{sc|Oracle|You've reached your destination, so just do what you have to do.<br/>Thank you for trusting me.}}
{{sc|Theresa|It may be a little late for this... but I'm glad to meet you.}}
{{sc|Oracle|I'm glad to meet you too, Theresa.}}
{{sc|Oracle walks into the distance of the endless wheat fields, disappearing within the stalks.<br/>A draft of wind tears through the plain with a roar, and the final scene disperses until only the end of a thread is left.<br/>Theresa holds the strand. It quickly loses its luster, and turns into powdery dust.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresa|It's time to say goodbye...<br/>We'll meet again in the future, won't we...?<br/>Kal'tsit... Amiya...}}
{{sc|Theresa pauses for a long while.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresa|......{nickname}.}}
{{sc|fades to white|mode=background}}
{{sc|Cloudy Skies|mode=image}}
{{sc|Theresa lets go of the final strand of thread in her hand, and watches it disperse and fade away like starlight.<br/>She takes a step forward, towards hope...<br/>Towards death.|mode=speech}}
